{{Top}}
[[File:ChancellorPalpatine-ToppsFinest2019.png|thumb|right|250px|Palpatine donned regal robes as the Republic's Supreme Chancellor.]]
'''Robes''', also known as '''cowls''', were loose-fitting [[Clothing|clothes]] with sleeves. The [[Jedi]] and [[Sith]] both often wore robes beneath a [[cloak]], and the Jedi had their own particular [[Jedi apparel|style]] of robes. [[Darth Sidious]] wore a hooded [[zeyd-cloth]] robe,<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> while [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] and the [[Emperor's Royal Guard|Imperial Guard]] wore robes with [[armor]].<ref name="RotJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> [[Jawa]]s wore robes with a hooded cowl.<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> Folding one's hands in front of them, such that they were obscured by their robes, was considered the most formal way one Jedi could address another.<ref name="Master & Apprentice">''[[Master & Apprentice]]''</ref>

Part of traditional [[Gatalenta]]n attire including [[Color|scarlet]] robes which was the only colourful part of the attire as the Gatalentan people were known for living austerely and wearing only pale grey or white clothing.<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref>

[[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] often wore the simple, white robes of a [[princess]], which helped to keep her enemies off guard.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars New Edition">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> She also had a blue robe that she wore<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" /> in [[3 BBY]]<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa's]] birth in [[19 BBY]]. The events of ''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]'' commence just after Organa's sixteenth [[birthday]], which places the events of the novel in [[3 BBY]].</ref> when sneaking around the [[Royal Palace of Alderaan]] to find out more information on the growing rebellion by looking through the royal accounts. Her adoptive father, [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail]], owned a dark green robe that had become almost shabby over time.<ref name="Leia Princess of Alderaan" />

During the [[High Republic Era]], civilian robes were common for noncombatants who participated in Jedi missions.<ref name="DayAcolyte">{{Acolyte|Day (episode)}}</ref> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Acolyte Timeline">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> the [[human]] [[Verosha Aniseya]] "Osha" and the [[Tynnan]] [[Bazil]] both wore civilian robes while on the [[mission to Khofar]]. Although Osha was originally reluctant to wear the robe, she eventually donned the outfit.<ref name="DayAcolyte" />

{{Clothes-stub}}

